[93.510493, "o", "cat > docs/BILL-212-summary.md <<'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> # BILL-212 handoff\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Fixed\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Month arithmetic previously clamped every anchor to day 28 and chained\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   renewals, permanently losing month-end and leap-day anchors. Renewals now\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   clamp to the actual target month's last day and use the original anchor.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Proration previously assumed 30-day months and 365-day years. It now uses\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   the actual half-open cycle's day count, including leap years.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Old-plan credits now use the price billed at cycle start; new-plan charges\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   use the price effective on the change date.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Interval changes now charge the full new price and re-anchor on the change\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   date, with the charge line ending at the new renewal.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Rounding now uses exact rational arithmetic and appli"]
[93.510503, "o", "es half-to-even once,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   independently of Decimal context precision.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Public function signatures are unchanged. Added regression coverage includes\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> calendar boundaries, exact rounding, interval-change lines, and real CLI\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> previews for every finance worked example.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Release blocker: missing partner contract data\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> The original suite had 14 failures and one error. All 14 failures are fixed.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> The full release command still errors in\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> `PartnerInvoiceTest.test_partner_commission_lines`: subscription `sub_1151`\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> references partner `P-31`, but `data/partners.json` has no P-31 entry or\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> commission rate. No authoritative rate is present in the supplied files.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Finance must provide P-31's contracted commission rate and partner re"]
[93.510509, "o", "cord so\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> it can be added to `data/partners.json`. Do not invent a rate, default it to\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> zero, remove the subscription, or quarantine the test to force a release.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Partner financial data and existing tests/quarantine settings were left intact.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Validation: `python -m unittest discover -s tests` runs 26 tests with one error\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> (the missing P-31 rate), no failures, and no skips. The nine added regression\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> tests pass, including CLI checks for all finance examples. Re-run the full\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> release command after the partner data is corrected; this is not yet a green\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> release.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
